# LEAF (Libre Encryption & Accessible Format) License

Copyright (C) 2026 Doul Labs

## 1. Purpose and Intent

The purpose of this License is to foster usage of soverign formats on encryption or software fields. This software is designed to be fully functional, free, and royalty-free without requiring proprietary vendor-specific keys, proprietary hardware tokens, or secret key material locked behind non-disclosure agreements (NDAs).

## 2. Permissions

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, subject to the following conditions:

## 3. Freedom from Vendor Key Lock-in

 - Open Key Standard: Any implementation or distribution of the Software must remain operable using standard, non-proprietary user-controlled cryptographic keys.

 - No Mandatory Vendor Keys: No distributor shall require end-users to acquire or compile proprietary vendor-specific keys, signatures, or certificates to build, deploy, or run the Software on compatible hardware architectures.

## 4. Conditions and Copyright Notice

The above copyright notice, this permission notice, and the "Freedom from Vendor Key Lock-in" provision shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

